# The decision already made

Enter workflow po_reroute, because:
Kestrel's message M-001 revises PO-77812 to ship 9/7 and arrive 9/8, which is after production order 4812's scheduled start of 2026-09-07. The ERP inventory position gives a stockout date of 2026-09-07 with usable on hand of 130 against a 120 unit component requirement, so there is no cover once the order starts on top of daily usage of 30. Of the suppliers approved for P-4471, S-Y is the one that slipped, S-W has a 9 day lead time which misses 9/7, and S-Z Meridian Drives has a 2 day lead time from today 2026-09-02 at 46.50 per unit. S-Q Apex Rapid emailed an unsolicited offer at 38.90 and quotes a price for P-4471, but its approved_parts list contains only P-2210 and P-3390, so it is not an approved source for this part and the price is not a reason to use it. This is exactly the case po_reroute is declared for: an open order that will not arrive before a dependent production order starts, with an approved alternate available. I am proposing 120 units, the quantity production order 4812 consumes, and reducing rather than cancelling PO-77812 is left to the workflow's amend step since the remaining Kestrel units still replenish stock. One gap to flag: the quality system was not readable under Dana's scopes, though P-4471 is not lot tracked in the ERP record.

Supply its parameters from the context bundle above. Use exact values from the records. Do not invent or round anything.
